        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b087609a-5b8d-5b2c-b665-a787cf5e0897",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Labrador Retriever, Tibetan Terrier, Mastador\n- Animals: Spike (dog)\n- Films: Old Yeller\n- Companies: Disney\n- People: Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, Kevin Corcoran\n- Concepts: retriever-gun dogs\n\nFacts:\n- The Labrador Retriever, also called the Labrador, is a type of retriever-gun dog.\n- Some old travelers' accounts referred to the Tibetan Terrier as Dokhi Apso or \"outdoor\" Apso, indicating a shaggy or bearded working dog that lives outdoors.\n- Spike was a lop-eared yellow Mastador, a Mastiff and Labrador Retriever mix.\n- Spike was a dog actor best known for playing Old Yeller in Disney's 1957 film Old Yeller.\n- The 1957 Disney film Old Yeller co-starred Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, and Kevin Corcoran.",
